<![CDATA[ASBA (Application Supported by Blocked Amount) is a facility provided by banks to investors in Initial Public Offerings (IPO's), Follow-on Public Offers (FPO's) and New Fund Offers (NFO's) of mutual funds.]]>
</TextElement>
<FieldProperty X="6" Y="180" Width="549" Height="28" VLine="0" VLineColor="-16777216"/>
<TextElement ID="Text115" Alignment="1" Indent="0.0" Hindent="0" Spacing="0" Visible="true" HideOnPrint="false" KeepWithNext="false" Font="Arial-PLAIN-9" Foreground="-16777216" FillStyle="0" TabStops="0.5,1.0,1.5,2.0,2.5,3.0,3.5,4.0,4.5,5.0,5.5,6.0,6.5,7.0,7.5,8.0" Justify="true" Orphan="false" TextAdvance="3">
<property><name><![CDATA[adjust.height]]></name><value><![CDATA[false]]></value></property>
<property><name><![CDATA[grow]]></name><value><![CDATA[false]]></value></property>
<![CDATA[If you apply for an IPO/NFO via ASBA, your application amount gets blocked in your bank account. While the amount stays in bank account, it cannot be withdrawn until the share/MF unit allotment is done. The money will be debited from your bank account only if your application is selected for allotment. The sum to be debited shall depend on the number of shares/MF units allotted to you and the remaining amount, if any, shall be unblocked in due course and shall continue at RBL Bank’s card rate, unless withdrawn.]]>
</TextElement>
